ull,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":97593,"output_tokens":3450,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"a2d738974a8d2231ee7bf99f5f1f1470487a600d7c9f727f2ecbe35be272668a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":35632,"output_tokens":1636,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test/AC asserting a candidate span opened inside a copy_context-propagated fan-out pool task shares the run span's trace id, so the parallel-propagation claim is exercised, not just main-context spans.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Contextvar propagation into the parallel fan-out already works (generation._submit_ctx runs each pool task under copy_context()), so no threading work is required.'","AC1: 'Two candidate spans opened within one gate run share a trace id' — does not specify the spans are opened inside a copy_context pool task, so the parallel path can go untested."],"finding":"The plan's one-trace outcome for the fan-out depends on contextvar propagation into parallel pool tasks (`generation._submit_ctx` / `copy_context()`), but no acceptance criterion asserts that a candidate span opened INSIDE a fan-out pool task shares the run span's trace id. The happy-path AC ('two candidate spans opened within one gate run') can pass with spans opened on the main context, leaving the actual parallel-propagation path — the load-bearing claim — unexercised.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f803d1b3171263b55","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Acceptance Criteria (happy-path AC line 1)","norm_id":"n216cc9924802c038","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future change to the pool submissi