n_workflow lives in _run_code_review_gate (gate_dispatch.py:492, with-block at :523)","Plan correctly notes this boundary 'opens no gate_config/with_identity' but still cites :372 as the edit location"],"finding":"The plan names produce_code_review_verdict (:372) as the third gate-run boundary to enclose with the run span, but that function is a 3-line orchestrator (preflight -> assemble -> _run_code_review_gate); the actual run + fan-out executes inside the `with` block of the helper _run_code_review_gate (:492, with-block at :523). Naming :372 as the enclosure site is imprecise: the span must wrap the executor.run_workflow call in _run_code_review_gate, not the orchestrator, to actually parent the candidate spans.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f54c93f0013051705","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section / AC line 3 — 'src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py ... :372 code-review'","norm_id":"n8c5d132056be8983","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author opens the span at :372 around the orchestrator call, which does correctly enclose the helper — so parentage may still hold — but the load-bearing 'ENCLOSE not sit inside' guidance is stated only for the two gate_config sites, leaving the code-review helper's exact insertion point unspecified."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State that for the code-review boundary the span encloses the produce_code_review_verdict orchestrator call (which transitively wraps _run_code_review_gate:523), or place it directly around the with-block at :523; note :372 is a 3-line delegator.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigatio